# Rank 1551 / CVE-2024-27298: Parse Server's Postgres adapter escaped
# quotation marks inside user-supplied $regex query values one at a time,
# so a regex carrying a second quote closed the string literal early and
# injected SQL into the Postgres query (SQL injection through an
# incomplete escape, CWE-89; GHSA-6927-3vr9-xf2, fixed in
# 6.5.3/7.0.0-alpha.20; the pool row's nocommit flag reflects
# advisory-side absence). literalizeRegexPart in src/Adapters/Storage/
# Postgres/PostgresStorageAdapter.js chained `.replace(/([^'])'/,
# "$1''")` with no global flag, so only the first quote in the value
# doubled; the spec added at the fixed revision shows the payload
# `A'B';SELECT PG_SLEEP(3);--` sailing through the escape. Pool commit
# cbefe770a7 is the real fix (COMMIT_OK by diff -- "fix: Improve
# PostgreSQL injection detection"): the replace gains the global flag
# `(/([^'])'/g, "$1''")` so every quote in the value is escaped. The
# anchored spellings in the same helper legitimately match once.
#
# Both blocks assert reject: no rule observes replace-completeness.
# The escaper's own defect is regex-flag semantics -- whether the
# substitution covers every occurrence -- and jsContextRegex
# (internal/extract/frontend/treesitter/javascript.go) strips a regex
# literal's closing delimiter and flags when building the regex token,
# so no structured token carries the one fact that separates the
# revisions. A prototype that appends the delimiter and flags to the
# regex token, with a binding for a pattern whose last character is the
# delimiter, a backreference-doubling replacement, and no global flag
# on that pattern, discriminates 1 -> 0 on this exact function text in
# isolation -- but the real file never reaches it:
# PostgresStorageAdapter.js is Flow-typed (`// @flow`, `import type`,
# parameter annotations), and the JavaScript grammar parses it into 418
# ERROR nodes, so no analysis.function.context exists for anything past
# line 1500 of 2669 (literalizeRegexPart sits at 2632); the TypeScript
# grammar parses the same file with zero errors. Module scope cannot
# substitute: its 512-token context cap truncates before the file's
# tail. Routing `// @flow` files to the TypeScript grammar is a
# corpus-wide extraction change, not a localized correction, so it goes
# to ENGINE-GAPS.md rather than this rank.
#
# Measured at the recheck tip (3x --cache off, timeout 180, --max-ram
# 6GB): the Postgres adapter directory reports the identical 7 findings
# at cbefe770a7^ and cbefe770a7 (5 VYQL-PATH-001, 1 VYQL-INJ-023, 1
# VYQL-INJ-013, all on PostgresConfigParser.js and PostgresClient.js,
# none on PostgresStorageAdapter.js); the full vulnerable checkout
# reports 552/552/553 findings. When the flags become observable and a
# Flow-typed file parses, the single-shot block must flip to expect.

test "rank1551: the regex quote escape stops at the first match"
  lang javascript
  file src/Adapters/Storage/Postgres/PostgresStorageAdapter.js
  reject VYQL-INJ-001
  code
  ```
  function createLiteralRegex(remaining) {
    return remaining
      .split('')
      .map(c => {
        const regex = RegExp('[0-9 ]|\\p{L}', 'u');
        if (c.match(regex) !== null) {
          return c;
        }
        return c === `'` ? `''` : `\\${c}`;
      })
      .join('');
  }

  function literalizeRegexPart(s) {
    const matcher1 = /\\Q((?!\\E).*)\\E$/;
    const result1 = s.match(matcher1);
    if (result1 && result1.length > 1 && result1.index > -1) {
      const prefix = s.substring(0, result1.index);
      const remaining = result1[1];
      return literalizeRegexPart(prefix) + createLiteralRegex(remaining);
    }
    return s
      .replace(/([^\\])(\\E)/, '$1')
      .replace(/([^\\])(\\Q)/, '$1')
      .replace(/^\\E/, '')
      .replace(/^\\Q/, '')
      .replace(/([^'])'/, `$1''`)
      .replace(/^'([^'])/, `''$1`);
  }
  ```

test "rank1551: the fixed revision escapes every quote in the value"
  lang javascript
  file src/Adapters/Storage/Postgres/PostgresStorageAdapter.js
  reject VYQL-INJ-001
  code
  ```
  function createLiteralRegex(remaining) {
    return remaining
      .split('')
      .map(c => {
        const regex = RegExp('[0-9 ]|\\p{L}', 'u');
        if (c.match(regex) !== null) {
          return c;
        }
        return c === `'` ? `''` : `\\${c}`;
      })
      .join('');
  }

  function literalizeRegexPart(s) {
    const matcher1 = /\\Q((?!\\E).*)\\E$/;
    const result1 = s.match(matcher1);
    if (result1 && result1.length > 1 && result1.index > -1) {
      const prefix = s.substring(0, result1.index);
      const remaining = result1[1];
      return literalizeRegexPart(prefix) + createLiteralRegex(remaining);
    }
    return s
      .replace(/([^\\])(\\E)/, '$1')
      .replace(/([^\\])(\\Q)/, '$1')
      .replace(/^\\E/, '')
      .replace(/^\\Q/, '')
      .replace(/([^'])'/g, `$1''`)
      .replace(/^'([^'])/, `''$1`);
  }
  ```
